From c884b01ca3fef8ffdbbcd4eae0c8c9fd265d03fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:13:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] debug: present-synchronized frame recorder + PGXP culling
 diagnostics

Lab diagnostics only - no rendering behavior changes.

framerec: {"cmd":"framerec","dir":D,"count":N,"div":K} captures the next N
presented frames from the completed backbuffer right before SwapWindow,
box-downsampled by K (default 2) and written as frame_NNNNN.png. Unlike
screenshot_hires (which reads the render target and can catch a half-drawn
frame), every file is exactly what the player saw for one game frame - the
tool for capturing per-frame wobble on a user's machine.

NCLIP culling-correction telemetry in the "pgxp" reply: nclip_precise /
nclip_gated counters, nclip_gate_why[dead,no-xy,no-z,value] classifying why
a vertex fell back to the integer winding, a lab-only nclip_noz toggle
(accept no-z vertices; measured: no effect), and noz_dump (ring of no-z
gated slots with writer provenance). Tri-ring records gain per-vertex
write age and writer pc; dead-LWC2 probe reports write provenance.
